Exercise: sa-logs-review (chapter 11 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root.

Journal
 1. Make the journal persistent: create /var/log/journal, and add a drop-in
    /etc/systemd/journald.conf.d/10-retention.conf with
    Storage=persistent and SystemMaxUse=100M. Restart systemd-journald and run journalctl --flush.

An application log
 2. /etc/rsyslog.d/10-appserver.conf sending the facility local6 (every
    priority) to /var/log/appserver.log. Restart rsyslog.
 3. Send the message "drill complete" to it with logger, using facility
    local6, and make sure it arrived in the file.
 4. /etc/logrotate.d/appserver: rotate that file weekly, keep 6 copies and
    compress them.

Time
 5. Set the time zone to Asia/Colombo.
 6. Add the line "server 0.pool.ntp.org iburst" to /etc/chrony.conf and
    restart chronyd. It must stay running and enabled.

On workstation
 7. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-logs-review
